357	 * date (its due-by plus its grace plus 30, 60, 90 ... days) of its figure plus the charges of the boundaries before it (compounding), each rounded to two decimals by the claim's rounding (see Rounding), added up; a
358	 * boundary whose percent is 0.00 adds nothing. A statement binds the claim's due as shown, the charge included: while
359	 * bound it no longer follows today (see #add); settling freezes it into the claim's due.
360	 * A claim whose late charge a steward waived bears none (see ApplyWaive).
361	 * The floor is applied first: a claim's live due is its figure floored (the greater of it and the floor in force on its date)
362	 * plus the charge worked out on that floored figure.
363	 */
364	public record LateCharge(LocalDate today, Function<LocalDate, BigDecimal> pct, Rounding rounding,
365	        Function<Claim, Integer> grace, java.util.function.Predicate<Claim> waived) {
366	
367	    /** The days in each step of the charge. */
368	    public static final int DAYS = 30;
369	
370	    public static LateCharge of(String sheetId, SheetRepository sheets, SettingRepository settings,
371	            ClaimRepository claims) {
372	        return new LateCharge(sheets.today(sheetId), (date) -> settings.latePct(sheetId, date),
373	                Rounding.of(sheetId, sheets, settings, claims),
374	                (claim) -> settings.graceOf(sheetId, claim.personId(), claim.date()),
375	                waivedIn(claims.waived(sheetId, null)));
